    "title": "IDENTIFIED: Woman killed in Fresno County crash into truck carrying classroom - NewsBreak",
    "text": "By Miranda Adams ,\n4 hours ago\nNOTE: The video in this story is from an earlier report.\nFRESNO COUNTY, Calif. ( KSEE/KGPE ) – The woman who was killed after crashing into a semi-truck Monday morning has been identified by the coroner’s office.\nThey named her as 43-year-old Elsa Gonzales of Fresno.\nAccording to CHP, she was heading up Chestnut Avenue when she collided with the back left portion of a tractor-trailer that was making a left turn onto the road.\nThe impact sent the Acura northeast into the parking lots of Red Triangle Oil Company and Flyers Filling Station, before swerving back onto the roadway. The driver was pronounced dead at the scene.\nThe driver of the commercial vehicle was not injured.\nAnyone with information is encouraged to contact the California Highway Patrol Fresno Area office at (559) 705-2200.\nCopyright 2026 Nexstar Media, Inc. All rights reserved. This material may not be published, broadcast, rewritten, or redistributed. For the latest news, weather, sports, and streaming video, head to CBS47 and KSEE24 | News from YourCentralValley.com.\n1",
    "summary": "FRESNO COUNTY, Calif. ( KSEE/KGPE ) – The woman who was killed after crashing into a semi-truck Monday morning has been identified by the coroner’s office. According to CHP, she was heading up Chestnut Avenue when she collided with the back left portion of a tractor-trailer that was making a left turn onto the road. The impact sent the Acura northeast into the parking lots of Red Triangle Oil Company and Flyers Filling Station, before swerving back onto the roadway. Anyone with information is encouraged to contact the California Highway Patrol Fresno Area office at (559) 705-2200.",
